Weakens ReadCacheSlot::release from release to relaxed. The store publishes
a reader's writes to its cache entry to the scrape, which runs on a writer's
thread and may delete the entry. The replacement for the mmap_end_ mutation:
same class (a weakened release/acquire pair), but one that carries data, so
only a concurrent run can see it. Expected: caught.
Sanitizer: thread
diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index baca3a34..5a6a43b8 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -853,7 +853,7 @@ public:
     return is_entry(e) ? e : nullptr;
   }
   void release(ReadCacheEntry *e) noexcept {
-    ptr_.store(e, std::memory_order_release);
+    ptr_.store(e, std::memory_order_relaxed);
   }
 
 private:
